  "schema": "ld-s10y-image/figure-spec@2",
  "id": "fig-choice-n42-six-graphs",
  "mode": "deterministic",
  "description": "Read horizontal intersection coordinates and compare function heights on actual framed graphs.",
  "source": {
    "authoredBasis": "New written-source graph sheet, not an original. Six separate complete frames A-F each plot y=x^2. Their lines are respectively -3x+4,2x+5,-2x-5,x/2+3/2,-2x/3+5/3,-12x/5+2. These divide every term by the original leading coefficient when needed. Root abscissas are respectively {-4,1},{1-sqrt(6),1+sqrt(6)},none,{-1,3/2},{-5/3,1},{(-6-sqrt(86))/5,(-6+sqrt(86))/5}. Exact quadratic Bezier paths, not guessed curves. No root labels, highlighted answers, or deliberate false geometry.",
    "authoritativeText": [
      {
        "lesson": "alg7-c4-s3-n42",
        "exercise": "853",
        "text": "853. 用图解法解下列方程：\na) $x^2+3x-4=0$；\nb) $x^2-2x-5=0$；\nc) $x^2+2x+5=0$；\nd) $2x^2-x-3=0$；\ne) $3x^2+2x-5=0$；\nf) $5x^2+12x-10=0$。"
      }
    ],
